<tool id="neutrons_radar_pd_model_campaign_prototype" name="RADAR-PD Utility: Model Campaign" version="0.2.17" profile="22.05">
    <description>run reviewed structural or magnetic model starts with bounded resources</description>
    <requirements><container type="docker">@IMMUTABLE_MODEL_IMAGE@</container></requirements>
    <command detect_errors="exit_code"><![CDATA[
        touch '$result_bundle' '$console_output' '$preparation_certificate' &&
        trap "chmod a+r '$result_bundle' '$console_output' '$preparation_certificate' >/dev/null 2>&1 || true" EXIT &&
        #if $model_request_b64 and $model_request
            echo 'Supply exactly one reviewed request source' >&2; exit 1
        #elif $model_request_b64
            python '$request_decoder' '$inline_request' decoded-model-request.json &&
            python /opt/radar-symmetry/ndip_model_campaign.py '$action' '$source_gpx' '$model_assets' decoded-model-request.json worker '$result_bundle' --preparation-evidence '$preparation_provenance' --preparation-certificate '$preparation_certificate' > '$console_output' 2>&1 &&
            python -m gpx_recipe.preparation.certificates '$preparation_certificate'
        #elif $model_request
            python /opt/radar-symmetry/ndip_model_campaign.py '$action' '$source_gpx' '$model_assets' '$model_request' worker '$result_bundle' --preparation-evidence '$preparation_provenance' --preparation-certificate '$preparation_certificate' > '$console_output' 2>&1 &&
            python -m gpx_recipe.preparation.certificates '$preparation_certificate'
        #else
            echo 'Supply one reviewed request source' >&2; exit 1
        #end if
    ]]></command>
    <configfiles>
        <configfile name="preparation_provenance"><![CDATA[#import json
#set records = []
#if $preparation_evidence
    #for certificate in $preparation_evidence
        #set dataset = $certificate.unsanitized
        #set job = getattr($dataset, 'creating_job', None)
        #set markers = [line for line in str(getattr($job, 'stdout', '')).splitlines() if line.startswith('[RADAR PREPARATION CERTIFICATE] ')]
        #set record = dict(certificate_path=str($certificate), tool_id=str(getattr($job, 'tool_id', '')), tool_version=str(getattr($job, 'tool_version', '')), job_state=str(getattr($job, 'state', '')), dataset_state=str(getattr($dataset, 'state', '')), dataset_deleted=bool(getattr($dataset, 'deleted', True)), dataset_purged=bool(getattr($dataset, 'purged', True)), job_stdout='\n'.join($markers))
        #set ignored = $records.append($record)
    #end for
#end if
$json.dumps(dict(schema='radar-galaxy-preparation-evidence/v1', records=$records), sort_keys=True)
]]></configfile>
        <configfile name="inline_request">$model_request_b64</configfile>
        <configfile name="request_decoder"><![CDATA[import base64, json, pathlib, sys
source, target = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])
if source.stat().st_size > 6 * 1024 * 1024:
    raise ValueError('Encoded model request exceeds its size bound')
raw = source.read_bytes().strip()
decoded = base64.b64decode(raw, validate=True)
if len(decoded) > 4 * 1024 * 1024:
    raise ValueError('Decoded model request exceeds its 4 MiB size bound')
if not isinstance(json.loads(decoded), dict):
    raise ValueError('A model request must be one JSON object')
if target.is_symlink():
    raise ValueError('The decoded request path must not be a symlink')
if target.exists():
    if target.read_bytes() != decoded:
        raise ValueError('A different request already occupies the decoded path')
else:
    with target.open('xb') as stream:
        stream.write(decoded)
]]></configfile>
    </configfiles>
    <inputs>
        <param name="action" type="select" label="Reviewed model operation">
            <option value="native">Inspect or prepare native models</option>
            <option value="chunk">Run a finite chunk of approved starts</option>
        </param>
        <param name="source_gpx" type="data" format="binary,txt" label="Exact source GPX or nuclear CIF (experiment preparation)"/>
        <param name="model_assets" type="data" format="zip" label="Captured scientific inputs"/>
        <param name="preparation_evidence" type="data" format="json" multiple="true" optional="true" label="Native preparation origin receipts (NOVA supplies these automatically)"/>
        <param name="model_request" type="data" format="json" optional="true" label="Reviewed model request dataset (legacy transport)"/>
        <param name="model_request_b64" type="text" value="" optional="true" label="NOVA encoded model request">
            <validator type="regex" message="Use the NOVA-generated base64 request">^[A-Za-z0-9+/=]*$</validator>
        </param>
        <param name="dispatch_key" type="text" label="NOVA dispatch identity">
            <validator type="regex" message="Use the NOVA-generated dispatch key">^[a-f0-9]{24}$</validator>
        </param>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="result_bundle" format="zip" label="RADAR-PD model ${dispatch_key} results"/>
        <data name="console_output" format="txt" label="RADAR-PD model ${dispatch_key} console"/>
        <data name="preparation_certificate" format="json" hidden="true" label="RADAR-PD native preparation receipt ${dispatch_key}"/>
        <collection name="verified_projects" type="list" label="Qualified model GPXs ${dispatch_key}">
            <discover_datasets pattern="verified_(?P&lt;designation&gt;[a-f0-9]+)\.gpx" ext="binary" directory="worker/verified_projects" visible="true"/>
        </collection>
        <collection name="reviewable_projects" type="list" label="Structural point-fit GPXs (review required) ${dispatch_key}">
            <discover_datasets pattern="reviewable_(?P&lt;designation&gt;[a-f0-9]+)\.gpx" ext="binary" directory="worker/reviewable_projects" visible="true"/>
        </collection>
    </outputs>
    <help><![CDATA[
NOVA captures the exact source GPX, candidate catalog and approved finite search.
The fast fixed-geometry magnetic optimizer prepares one subgroup in an isolated
process and screens its complete reviewed start portfolio against one checked
surrogate. Distinct calculated profiles are independently verified with GSAS-II.
Equivalent screened starts retain their own moment solutions and reference a
native-verified representative; they are not separate verified GPX files.
Other refinement modes retain independent fresh-process starts. Workers respect
GALAXY_SLOTS, memory and container CPU quotas; absent allocation information
permits one worker.
Unstarted trials remain pending at the chunk deadline. Every result retains its
disposition, source and protocol hashes. Only independently audited, qualified
projects appear in the output collection. A low Rwp does not establish a structure.
No model API credential, Galaxy key, Python script or network request is accepted
as an input. Discovery and planning run separately in NOVA.
NOVA can send the closed request as a sanitized base64 parameter, decoded into
a bounded JSON data file. The same native validation applies; no per-chunk
request upload is required. Existing uploaded JSON requests remain supported.
Independent starts share only the CPU and memory allocated to their Galaxy job.
NOVA separately limits concurrent batches across scans; visible host cores do
not authorize additional native workers.
Experiment preparation can instead supply one nuclear CIF with captured bank
profiles and a closed preparation request. The worker creates theoretical
reference calculations without fitting observations. Its portable result bundle
contains data only; preparation does not create a verified experimental GPX.
Structural acquisition requests use the same reviewed complete-mode engine as
completed-scan model exploration. Their separate point-fit collection contains
independently checked GPX exports for inspection and continuation; it does not
assert optimization convergence, a unique structure or a posterior probability.
The source parameter keeps its existing name for compatibility. Text includes
plain CIF uploads; native operations verify the selected source's content and
exact checksum before scientific use.
The native wrapper emits a compact origin receipt and announces its digest to
Galaxy's job stdout. Subsequent jobs receive creating-job metadata from this
fixed template, separately from uploaded request data. Exact-context structural
banks can then retain the complete precomputed portfolio after fresh native
probes. Missing, modified, incompatible or uploaded-only origin records retain
native reconstruction. Receipts contain no API keys or experimental patterns;
they do not certify an experimental fit or authorize a changed physical context.
    ]]></help>
</tool>
